{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '150,190p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '153,215p' ../agent-source/raftpb/raft.proto; sed -n '340,448p' ../agent-source/rawnode_test.go; sed -n '120,185p' ../agent-source/quorum/majority.go; cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md\"","aggregated_output":"\t// message is only allowed if all Nodes participating in the cluster run a\n\t// version of this library aware of the V2 API. See pb.ConfChangeV2 for\n\t// usage details and semantics.\n\tProposeConfChange(ctx context.Context, cc pb.ConfChangeI) error\n\n\t// Step advances the state machine using the given message. ctx.Err() will be returned, if any.\n\tStep(ctx context.Context, msg pb.Message) error\n\n\t// Ready returns a channel that returns the current point-in-time state.\n\t// Users of the Node must call Advance after retrieving the state returned by Ready (unless\n\t// async storage writes is enabled, in which case it should never be called).\n\t//\n\t// NOTE: No committed entries from the next Ready may be applied until all committed entries\n\t// and snapshots from the previous one have finished.\n\tReady() <-chan Ready\n\n\t// Advance notifies the Node that the application has saved progress up to the last Ready.\n\t// It prepares the node to return the next available Ready.\n\t//\n\t// The application should generally call Advance after it applies the entries in last Ready.\n\t//\n\t// However, as an optimization, the application may call Advance while it is applying the\n\t// commands. For example. when the last Ready contains a snapshot, the application might take\n\t// a long time to apply the snapshot data. To continue receiving Ready without blocking raft\n\t// progress, it can call Advance before finishing applying the last ready.\n\t//\n\t// NOTE: Advance must not be called when using AsyncStorageWrites. Response messages from the\n\t// local append and apply threads take its place.\n\tAdvance()\n\t// ApplyConfChange applies a config change (previously passed to\n\t// ProposeConfChange) to the node. This must be called whenever a config\n\t// change is observed in Ready.CommittedEntries, except when the app decides\n\t// to reject the configuration change (i.e. treats it as a noop instead), in\n\t// which case it must not be called.\n\t//\n\t// Returns an opaque non-nil ConfState protobuf which must be recorded in\n\t// snapshots.\n\tApplyConfChange(cc pb.ConfChangeI) *pb.ConfState\n\n\t// TransferLeadership attempts to transfer leadership to the given transferee.\n\tTransferLeadership(ctx context.Context, lead, transferee uint64)\nenum ConfChangeType {\n\tConfChangeAddNode        = 0;\n\tConfChangeRemoveNode     = 1;\n\tConfChangeUpdateNode     = 2;\n\tConfChangeAddLearnerNode = 3;\n}\n\nmessage ConfChange {\n\toptional ConfChangeType  type    = 2 [(gogoproto.nullable) = false];\n\toptional uint64          node_id = 3 [(gogoproto.nullable) = false, (gogoproto.customname) = \"NodeID\"];\n\toptional bytes           context = 4;\n\n\t// NB: this is used only by etcd to thread through a unique identifier.\n\t// Ideally it should really use the Context instead. No counterpart to\n\t// this field exists in ConfChangeV2.\n\toptional uint64          id      = 1 [(gogoproto.nullable) = false, (gogoproto.customname) = \"ID\"];\n}\n\n// ConfChangeSingle is an individual configuration change operation. Multiple\n// such operations can be carried out atomically via a ConfChangeV2.\nmessage ConfChangeSingle {\n\toptional ConfChangeType  type    = 1 [(gogoproto.nullable) = false];\n\toptional uint64          node_id = 2 [(gogoproto.nullable) = false, (gogoproto.customname) = \"NodeID\"];\n}\n\n// ConfChangeV2 messages initiate configuration changes. They support both the\n// simple \"one at a time\" membership change protocol and full Joint Consensus\n// allowing for arbitrary changes in membership.\n//\n// The supplied context is treated as an opaque payload and can be used to\n// attach an action on the state machine to the application of the config change\n// proposal. Note that contrary to Joint Consensus as outlined in the Raft\n// paper[1], configuration changes become active when they are *applied* to the\n// state machine (not when they are appended to the log).\n//\n// The simple protocol can be used whenever only a single change is made.\n//\n// Non-simple changes require the use of Joint Consensus, for which two\n// configuration changes are run. The first configuration change specifies the\n// desired changes and transitions the Raft group into the joint configuration,\n// in which quorum requires a majority of both the pre-changes and post-changes\n// configuration. Joint Consensus avoids entering fragile intermediate\n// configurations that could compromise survivability. For example, without the\n// use of Joint Consensus and running across three availability zones with a\n// replication factor of three, it is not possible to replace a voter without\n// entering an intermediate configuration that does not survive the outage of\n// one availability zone.\n//\n// The provided ConfChangeTransition specifies how (and whether) Joint Consensus\n// is used, and assigns the task of leaving the joint configuration either to\n// Raft or the application. Leaving the joint configuration is accomplished by\n// proposing a ConfChangeV2 with only and optionally the Context field\n// populated.\n//\n// For details on Raft membership changes, see:\n//\n// [1]: https://github.com/ongardie/dissertation/blob/master/online-trim.pdf\nmessage ConfChangeV2 {\n\toptional ConfChangeTransition transition = 1 [(gogoproto.nullable) = false];\n\trepeated ConfChangeSingle     changes =    2 [(gogoproto.nullable) = false];\n\toptional bytes                context =    3;\n}\n\n// TestRawNodeJointAutoLeave tests the configuration change auto leave even leader\n// lost leadership.\nfunc TestRawNodeJointAutoLeave(t *testing.T) {\n\ttestCc := pb.ConfChangeV2{Changes: []pb.ConfChangeSingle{\n\t\t{Type: pb.ConfChangeAddLearnerNode, NodeID: 2},\n\t},\n\t\tTransition: pb.ConfChangeTransitionJointImplicit,\n\t}\n\texpCs := pb.ConfState{\n\t\tVoters: []uint64{1}, VotersOutgoing: []uint64{1}, Learners: []uint64{2},\n\t\tAutoLeave: true,\n\t}\n\texp2Cs := pb.ConfState{Voters: []uint64{1}, Learners: []uint64{2}}\n\n\ts := newTestMemoryStorage(withPeers(1))\n\trawNode, err := NewRawNode(newTestConfig(1, 10, 1, s))\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\n\trawNode.Campaign()\n\tproposed := false\n\tvar (\n\t\tlastIndex uint64\n\t\tccdata    []byte\n\t)\n\t// Propose the ConfChange, wait until it applies, save the resulting\n\t// ConfState.\n\tvar cs *pb.ConfState\n\tfor cs == nil {\n\t\trd := rawNode.Ready()\n\t\ts.Append(rd.Entries)\n\t\tfor _, ent := range rd.CommittedEntries {\n\t\t\tvar cc pb.ConfChangeI\n\t\t\tif ent.Type == pb.EntryConfChangeV2 {\n\t\t\t\tvar ccc pb.ConfChangeV2\n\t\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, ccc.Unmarshal(ent.Data))\n\t\t\t\tcc = &ccc\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif cc != nil {\n\t\t\t\t// Force it step down.\n\t\t\t\trawNode.Step(pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgHeartbeatResp, From: 1, Term: rawNode.raft.Term + 1})\n\t\t\t\tcs = rawNode.ApplyConfChange(cc)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\trawNode.Advance(rd)\n\t\t// Once we are the leader, propose a command and a ConfChange.\n\t\tif !proposed && rd.SoftState.Lead == rawNode.raft.id {\n\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, rawNode.Propose([]byte(\"somedata\")))\n\t\t\tccdata, err = testCc.Marshal()\n\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\t\t\trawNode.ProposeConfChange(testCc)\n\t\t\tproposed = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Check that the last index is exactly the conf change we put in,\n\t// down to the bits. Note that this comes from the Storage, which\n\t// will not reflect any unstable entries that we'll only be presented\n\t// with in the next Ready.\n\tlastIndex, err = s.LastIndex()\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\n\tentries, err := s.Entries(lastIndex-1, lastIndex+1, noLimit)\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\trequire.Len(t, entries, 2)\n\tassert.Equal(t, []byte(\"somedata\"), entries[0].Data)\n\trequire.Equal(t, pb.EntryConfChangeV2, entries[1].Type)\n\tassert.Equal(t, ccdata, entries[1].Data)\n\n\trequire.Equal(t, &expCs, cs)\n\n\trequire.Zero(t, rawNode.raft.pendingConfIndex)\n\n\t// Move the RawNode along. It should not leave joint because it's follower.\n\trd := rawNode.readyWithoutAccept()\n\t// Check that the right ConfChange comes out.\n\trequire.Empty(t, rd.Entries)\n\n\t// Make it leader again. It should leave joint automatically after moving apply index.\n\trawNode.Campaign()\n\trd = rawNode.Ready()\n\tt.Log(DescribeReady(rd, nil))\n\ts.Append(rd.Entries)\n\trawNode.Advance(rd)\n\trd = rawNode.Ready()\n\tt.Log(DescribeReady(rd, nil))\n\ts.Append(rd.Entries)\n\trawNode.Advance(rd)\n\trd = rawNode.Ready()\n\tt.Log(DescribeReady(rd, nil))\n\ts.Append(rd.Entries)\n\trawNode.Advance(rd)\n\trd = rawNode.Ready()\n\tt.Log(DescribeReady(rd, nil))\n\ts.Append(rd.Entries)\n\t// Check that the right ConfChange comes out.\n\trequire.Len(t, rd.Entries, 1)\n\trequire.Equal(t, pb.EntryConfChangeV2, rd.Entries[0].Type)\n\tvar cc pb.ConfChangeV2\n\trequire.NoError(t, cc.Unmarshal(rd.Entries[0].Data))\n\trequire.Equal(t, pb.ConfChangeV2{Context: nil}, cc)\n\t// Lie and pretend the ConfChange applied. It won't do so because now\n\t// we require the joint quorum and we're only running one node.\n\tcs = rawNode.ApplyConfChange(cc)\n\trequire.Equal(t, exp2Cs, *cs)\n}\n\n// TestRawNodeProposeAddDuplicateNode ensures that two proposes to add the same node should\n// not affect the later propose to add new node.\n\tif n == 0 {\n\t\t// This plays well with joint quorums which, when one half is the zero\n\t\t// MajorityConfig, should behave like the other half.\n\t\treturn math.MaxUint64\n\t}\n\n\t// Use an on-stack slice to collect the committed indexes when n <= 7\n\t// (otherwise we alloc). The alternative is to stash a slice on\n\t// MajorityConfig, but this impairs usability (as is, MajorityConfig is just\n\t// a map, and that's nice). The assumption is that running with a\n\t// replication factor of >7 is rare, and in cases in which it happens\n\t// performance is a lesser concern (additionally the performance\n\t// implications of an allocation here are far from drastic).\n\tvar stk [7]uint64\n\tvar srt []uint64\n\tif len(stk) >= n {\n\t\tsrt = stk[:n]\n\t} else {\n\t\tsrt = make([]uint64, n)\n\t}\n\n\t{\n\t\t// Fill the slice with the indexes observed. Any unused slots will be\n\t\t// left as zero; these correspond to voters that may report in, but\n\t\t// haven't yet. We fill from the right (since the zeroes will end up on\n\t\t// the left after sorting below anyway).\n\t\ti := n - 1\n\t\tfor id := range c {\n\t\t\tif idx, ok := l.AckedIndex(id); ok {\n\t\t\t\tsrt[i] = uint64(idx)\n\t\t\t\ti--\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tslices.Sort(srt)\n\n\t// The smallest index into the array for which the value is acked by a\n\t// quorum. In other words, from the end of the slice, move n/2+1 to the\n\t// left (accounting for zero-indexing).\n\tpos := n - (n/2 + 1)\n\treturn Index(srt[pos])\n}\n\n// VoteResult takes a mapping of voters to yes/no (true/false) votes and returns\n// a result indicating whether the vote is pending (i.e. neither a quorum of\n// yes/no has been reached), won (a quorum of yes has been reached), or lost (a\n// quorum of no has been reached).\nfunc (c MajorityConfig) VoteResult(votes map[uint64]bool) VoteResult {\n\tif len(c) == 0 {\n\t\t// By convention, the elections on an empty config win. This comes in\n\t\t// handy with joint quorums because it'll make a half-populated joint\n\t\t// quorum behave like a majority quorum.\n\t\treturn VoteWon\n\t}\n\n\tvar votedCnt int //vote counts for yes.\n\tvar missing int\n\tfor id := range c {\n\t\tv, ok := votes[id]\n\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\tmissing++\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif v {\n\t\t\tvotedCnt++\n\t\t}\n# File products for one audit investigation\n\nRead research.json for selected work and shared relationship navigation. A record locator names an existing JSON path, collection and exact match fields; paths are relative to the index directory unless absolute. Select matching records, then read field when present. Historical previews are navigation, not current pending work. Use artifact basis locators and graph_versions for old requirements, not the latest same-ID claim. Materials and execution IDs resolve through records in state.json. Full reviews, drafts and fixed inputs remain at their indexed paths.\n\nWhen capacity permits, supply an optional short Chinese report_title and one to three report_answer sentences in review items, leading with the measured discrepancy and actual observation. State decisive applicability once and keep open disputes visible; leave repeated execution detail and wider exclusions in the scoped records. Keep English semantic reasoning; actual verdicts and measurements prevail. Omission never blocks work or warrants a translation turn.\n\nWrite a complete submission.json using submission.schema.json and product-schemas.json. Cite authorized captured ranges. Follow next_objective and the analysis guide for core_overview readiness; a usable map and first Candidate may share a submission.\n\nWhen repairing a rejected product, set repair_of to its operation_id and submit the whole product. Diagnostics retain ownership: reconsider=submission calls for product repair; reconsider=research_decision requires a different research action, not field repair of an unauthorized stop. Repeated errors may pause only the draft, never unrelated questions.\n\n- continue / pause / explained / obligation: select candidate_id or fork using parent_candidate_id, with a complete current question. Sourced feedback may refine the discriminator before its first obligation; later requirement/scope changes use F2/F3. A fork explains holds/violated/incomplete effects on its parent. Pause supplies resume_conditions; explained cites the protective mechanism. Obligation supplies one attributed claim and source bindings. A complete check may be combined now, or constructed later.\n- check / revise_check: select unit_id (or its Candidate alias), or create an obligation through candidate. Supply plan_path, draft-source harness_path and optional destination-to-draft files; plan.harness.execution_package may select one Go package or Rust crate for this check. Metadata source/files stay empty; the controller fixes executable bytes and adapter support. Never replace target code or dependencies. Revisions name previous_check_id. Driver legality repairs name repair_issue_ids and explain changed inputs and sources; reference every removed conflict's exact issue. Changed executed checker encoding uses encoding_revision.\n- research: submit substantive feedback alone with acquired source or retained execution ref_ids, or a complete partial map_path, additive graph_path or scope_path. Feedback alone needs no Candidate or usable overview and creates no map version or Evidence. An identical adjacent pure handoff on unchanged research receives duplicate_of: accepted without new knowledge; continue useful investigation, not rewording. A map may accompany one graph/scope operation. semantic_revision supplies an attributed F2/F3 feedback_path for an existing unit_id and may carry a map. Graph additions cannot invent unowned executable Units.\n- review: select artifact_id; omitted item target_id inherits it. Carries feedback, not a map. Use review_contracts/review_questions: Direct Check requires checker_correspondence; other aspects are optional unless resolving an issue of that aspect. revision_needed names challenged_components. Resolve exact issue_ids using acquired Material source_ids, a concise answer and retained evidence_ids when relevant. For supplied conditions, use condition_dispositions with exact condition_id, sources and applicability; current_judgment remains unresolved. Unchanged sources and reasoning can be referenced, not recopied. The review guide defines semantic criteria. Candidate applicability review creates no execution Evidence.\n- explore: submit a question, draft-source harness_path, optional files and optional execution_package with the same meaning as Harness.execution_package. Clean-copy output guides construction without property Evidence.\n- stop: candidate/family/focus release local work; unfinished Units and disputes remain. A local tool/resource gap supplies resume_conditions. Open runs reject scope=run: continue with research, exploration or another Candidate within remaining authorization. Only a preconfigured finite directed_question may end with run/bounded_completed after its task is disposed; cite the explained, closed or checked Candidate. Cancellation, permission/service failure and exhausted time/calls are controller events, never submission authority.\n\nFor Go, omit execution_package to retain the run default package and main-file destination. An explicit local directory selects that package and places the primary file there using the configured basename. Helpers in files remain relative to the workspace root. The controller fixes the effective package and bytes before execution; it runs Go directly in a clean copy, without a root launcher. Select only one existing package in the captured module; paths, patterns, nested modules, workspaces and dependency overrides cannot expand authorization. Python does not support this override.\n\nFor Rust, execution_package selects one captured crate directory and tests/<configured basename>.rs, with workspace-relative helpers. Use research.build_inputs (fixed lock, tools, metadata and selected-test compilation) to check available APIs against effective features; a source declaration alone does not establish active cfg or public reachability. Original manifests and dev-dependencies determine features; no extra flags are added. Omit logging or helper initialization unrelated to the discriminator. The backend instructions describe private seed reuse and current harness execution; preparation consumes the run deadline and supplies no observations. Never replace manifests, locks, build scripts or tool configuration.\n\nA formal question names one principal fact_ids entry, lifecycle, direct behavior_ids, sourced A1/A2 relationship, contexts, event_paths, importance and trigger_rationale. supporting_behavior_ids maps distinct Behavior IDs to their causal role. audit_spec_version may be omitted for the current basis. A map file's version is its accepted base (1 initially); the controller assigns resulting versions, including questions in combined products and F2/F3 patches. Do not guess current+1. Unchanged Candidates retain their historical basis. A supporting-layer question cites its actual consumer or core relationship and declares the supported A1/A2 activity; a local storage obligation need not become a whole-cluster consequence. If that relationship lacks sources, investigate or retain feedback instead of inventing a core label.\n\nThe controller derives actual map differences and reverse indexes. map_changes explains modified/removed objects and new producers or consumers of an existing principal Fact, with impact (clarification/meaning/dependency), acquired source_ids and rationale. Use one preserves explanation for unchanged requirements, dependencies and observation scope, or challenges mapping saved Candidate IDs to specific disputed premises. A corrected principal Fact requires a challenge; clarification cannot disguise identity/context/edge changes or removal. Independent additions need no invented revision and may still challenge a prior interpretation.\n\nCoherent knowledge and its issues are accepted together; unaffected checks retain their basis. reconnect_questions updates explicitly selected questions. ScopeUpdate/F3 expands dependencies under its existing write rules; changed normative or fault/configuration applicability uses F2. No-op maps create no version.\n\nFor every feedback shape, including one accompanying a map, Candidate or review, ref_ids directly includes each saved CheckRun whose execution it explains, alongside relevant Candidate, Behavior, Fact, surface:<entry_point> and Material IDs. Obtain execution IDs from research.json.explorations[*].executions[*].check_id or the exact records locator, not operation/plan IDs or prose. Explaining only a repaired execution references only that run; a joint explanation references both failure and repair and distinguishes their observations. Shared sources, Behavior or harness names do not associate executions. Source-only answers need no execution reference. Map/map_changes source_ids remain Material references. understanding records learning, not a map change; use the guide's natural handoff. question_updates revises Candidate unknowns/resume_conditions with sources, retaining requirements and counterevidence. Historical remaining is then-remaining; current execution/review records remain authoritative.\n\nClaim/Scope owns requirement and applicability; Harness legality records this history and caller duties. Use the experiments reference for predicate correspondence, observation synchronization, prerequisite waits and cleanup responsibility during construction and review. Unreached setup retains its observation and calls for minimal repair preserving the discriminator. claim.concern classifies responsibility, not confidence.\n\nOptional preflight: run validation.command followed by the draft-relative filename in an existing Codex tool call. It shares acceptance preparation, writes no accepted state and executes no target; formal submission rechecks fixed bytes and current state without a preflight ticket. capacity is the current budget snapshot: new_obligation is an entry capability, not a complete check/review budget; remaining.agent_calls counts future turns, not local work in this running turn. A reliable receipt fixes only declared product files before deadline handling; saved bytes are not acceptance or Evidence. Without it, drafts remain unsubmitted. While time remains, an understood exploration answer may use feedback-only research under the same reference rule, retaining conditions, actual observations and remaining responsibility/history/endpoint questions. It need not wait for a map, Candidate or obligation to pass preflight. Keep rejected larger drafts and diagnostics separate; the small product neither repairs nor partially accepts them. Combine products when ready; no mandatory feedback turn or new deadline threshold. Natural expiry needs no closing submission.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_initial.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\ndef src(i,f,a,b,k='code_observation'):\n sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k));return i\nsrc('S_usage','doc.go',70,121,'document_statement')\nsrc('S_async_contract','doc.go',178,210,'document_statement')\nsrc('S_ready_contract','node.go',70,110,'interface_statement')\nsrc('S_node_contract','node.go',134,190,'interface_statement')\nsrc('S_conf_contract','raftpb/raft.proto',178,211,'interface_statement')\nsrc('S_restore_init','raft.go',437,496)\nsrc('S_send','raft.go',509,600)\nsrc('S_commit_reset','raft.go',692,848)\nsrc('S_auto_leave','raft.go',740,767)\nsrc('S_timers','raft.go',850,889)\nsrc('S_campaign','raft.go',891,1073)\nsrc('S_dispatch','raft.go',1085,1263)\nsrc('S_proposal','raft.go',1267,1385)\nsrc('S_ack','raft.go',1507,1607)\nsrc('S_transfer','raft.go',1608,1664)\nsrc('S_roles','raft.go',1668,1775)\nsrc('S_receive','raft.go',1786,1852)\nsrc('S_restore','raft.go',1857,1945)\nsrc('S_config','raft.go',1947,2031)\nsrc('S_reads','raft.go',2062,2084)\nsrc('S_read_release','raft.go',2123,2162)\nsrc('S_raw_ready','rawnode.go',118,190)\nsrc('S_raw_storage','rawnode.go',202,283)\nsrc('S_raw_completion','rawnode.go',368,495)\nsrc('S_log_append','log.go',107,142)\nsrc('S_log_apply','log.go',218,273)\nsrc('S_log_commit','log.go',320,364)\nsrc('S_log_context','log.go',440,469)\nsrc('S_joint','quorum/joint.go',17,77)\nsrc('S_tracker','tracker/tracker.go',26,119)\nsrc('S_tracker_commit','tracker/tracker.go',152,181)\nsrc('S_confchange','confchange/confchange.go',37,157)\nsrc('S_restore_config','confchange/restore.go',119,165)\nsrc('S_node_loop','node.go',349,460)\nsrc('S_status','status.go',24,80)\nsrc('S_read_queue','read_only.go',23,121)\nB=[]\ndef beh(i,a,owner,context,trigger,ss,**kw):\n b=dict(id=i,primary_activity=a,execution_owner=owner,protocol_context=context,trigger=trigger,source_ids=ss);b.update(kw);B.append(b)\nbeh('B_election','A2','raft.Step, hup, campaign, stepCandidate','Local node term and active voter configuration','Tick or Campaign, eligible vote requests and responses',['S_campaign','S_dispatch','S_roles','S_joint','S_send'],implementation_guards=['Campaign requires local voter eligibility, no pending snapshot, and no unapplied committed configuration change.','Vote eligibility uses recorded vote/current leader and candidate last log term/index; joint vote result requires both majorities.','Response type must match candidate versus pre-candidate phase.'],writes=['Real election increments term and records self vote; pre-election does neither.','Winning real votes installs leader and appends a current-term empty entry.'],external_effects=['Vote and append responses, including self-votes, await the storage completion path.'],produces_fact_ids=['F_authority'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_config'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Leader authority selects the term used to qualify replication support and new commitment.'})\nbeh('B_context_reset','A2','raft.Step, reset, becomeFollower','Node term, leader role and volatile aggregation','Higher-term message, accepted leader message while candidate, or failed quorum check',['S_dispatch','S_commit_reset','S_roles','S_proposal'],writes=['New term clears vote; resets election timers, vote tally, per-peer progress, pendingConfIndex, transfer target and readOnly heartbeat-ack queue.','Preserves raftLog and committed entries across role changes.'],important_branches=['Future pre-votes and successful pre-vote responses do not change local term; a recent leader lease may reject disruptive vote requests.','Lower-term protocol messages are ignored or answered with current term; old storage append completions cannot stabilize entries, but snapshot completion remains applicable.','pendingReadIndexMessages is not cleared by reset, unlike readOnly.'],produces_fact_ids=['F_authority'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Old replication support is not retained as current leader match evidence; established committed history survives.'},unknowns=['Determine whether retained pre-commit read requests can affect semantics after authority changes; no violation inferred from retention.'])\nbeh('B_replication','A1','stepLeader, handleAppendEntries, handleHeartbeat','Leader term, per-peer Match and local log prefix','Proposal, MsgApp, MsgAppResp, heartbeat and retry',['S_proposal','S_send','S_commit_reset','S_ack','S_receive','S_log_append','S_log_context','S_tracker_commit','S_joint'],implementation_guards=['Leader drops proposals during transfer or when its progress is absent; limits uncommitted bytes.','Follower requires matching previous entry term and forbids overwriting committed entries.','Leader uses configured quorum match index and only commits an index whose log term equals current term.'],writes=['Assigns proposal index/term; appends unstable entries; durable acknowledgements update Match; successful maybeCommit advances committed.'],external_effects=['Successful ack-driven commitment releases pending reads and broadcasts appends.','Heartbeat commit is capped at recipient Match; rejection/backoff and heartbeat responses resume replication.'],produces_fact_ids=['F_committed'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_authority','F_config'],async_boundaries=['Replication acknowledgements are queued until caller storage completion.'])\nbeh('B_storage_ready','A6','RawNode Ready/acceptReady/Advance and caller storage workers','Per-node Ready batches and term-tagged append completion','Ready acceptance and conventional Advance or asynchronous append/apply responses',['S_usage','S_async_contract','S_ready_contract','S_raw_ready','S_raw_storage','S_raw_completion','S_dispatch'],legal_preconditions=['Caller persists required state and preserves Ready processing order; async messages to each local worker are reliable and ordered.'],writes=['Tracks in-progress unstable writes and application batches; append completion removes matching stable entries; apply completion advances applied.'],external_effects=['Non-async Advance dispatches captured local responses; async Ready emits worker messages with dependent response lists.'],important_branches=['Async application only exposes locally stable committed entries; conventional application may use unstable entries under the Ready persistence contract.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_committed'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Persist-before-response makes acknowledgement support usable across crashes.','A2':'Term-tagged append completions distinguish old writes from current unstable state.','A5':'Ordered application completions update applied state and can trigger automatic configuration exit.'})\nbeh('B_application','A5','raft.appliedTo and raftLog application accounting','Committed/applied/applying indexes and configuration currently active at node','MsgStorageApplyResp, conventional Advance, or snapshot completion',['S_auto_leave','S_log_apply','S_log_commit','S_raw_completion','S_dispatch'],writes=['Advances applied monotonically and releases application byte pressure.'],important_branches=['When AutoLeave is true, applied reaches pendingConfIndex and this node is leader, proposes empty ConfChangeV2.','The proposal can be rejected while a leadership transfer is active; code relies on a later applied entry to retry.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_committed','F_config'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Automatic joint exit proposal determines when authority can transition from joint voters to incoming voters.'},unknowns=['Does caller-owned ordinary Ready processing guarantee another appliedTo callback after a transfer rejects the only automatic exit attempt?'])\nbeh('B_configuration','A4','raft.applyConfChange, switchToConfig and confchange.Changer','Applied ConfChangeV2 and active incoming/outgoing voter sets','Caller applies committed membership entry, or configuration is restored from snapshot',['S_node_contract','S_conf_contract','S_config','S_confchange','S_tracker','S_restore_config'],implementation_guards=['Simple changes alter at most one voter; EnterJoint refuses already-joint state; LeaveJoint requires outgoing voters.','Proposal admission serializes configuration changes behind applied pendingConfIndex and requires leaving joint state before another change.'],writes=['Installs incoming/outgoing voters, learners and staged learners; sets AutoLeave on EnterJoint and clears it on LeaveJoint.'],important_branches=['Leader removal/demotion may step down depending on StepDownOnRemoval; otherwise proposals are constrained separately.','switchToConfig reevaluates commitment and broadcasts if it changes, but does not call releasePendingReadIndexMessages.'],produces_fact_ids=['F_config','F_committed'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Installed joint voter sets determine eligible acknowledgement and vote quorums.','A2':'Applied configuration changes determine eligibility for future campaigns and transferred leadership.'},unknowns=['Reachability of a first-current-term commitment caused by switchToConfig while an earlier read is pending needs history analysis.'])\nbeh('B_transfer','A2','stepLeader MsgTransferLeader, tickHeartbeat, abortLeaderTransfer','Current leader and eligible transferee progress','Transfer request, transferee catch-up, timeout, or transferee removal',['S_transfer','S_timers','S_config','S_roles'],implementation_guards=['Ignores learners/self transfers; catch-up uses tracked Match before TimeoutNow.'],writes=['Sets leadTransferee and resets electionElapsed; clears target on timeout or invalidated membership.'],external_effects=['Sends append to catch up transferee or TimeoutNow to initiate real election.'],important_branches=['While leadTransferee is nonzero, proposals are dropped, including internally proposed joint exits.','Timeout aborts transfer but does not itself call appliedTo or append an entry.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_authority','F_config'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Proposal admission is paused during transfer, then restored on abort.'})\nbeh('B_recovery','A3','newRaft, restore, handleSnapshot','Stored HardState, snapshot configuration and committed prefix','Construction/restart or snapshot receipt',['S_restore_init','S_restore','S_receive','S_restore_config','S_log_context'],implementation_guards=['Obsolete snapshots are ignored; receiver membership is required.','Matching snapshot log term permits commit fast-forward without replacing the log; otherwise restore replaces unstable history and reconstructs configuration.'],writes=['Reconstructs configuration and committed position; initializes follower role.'],produces_fact_ids=['F_config','F_committed'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Committed prefix and restored membership constrain subsequent quorum formation.','A2':'Pending snapshot prevents campaign until its completion; snapshot completion remains valid across term changes.'})\nbeh('B_reads','A7','stepLeader/stepFollower ReadIndex and readOnly queue','Request context, leader term, committed index and active voters','ReadIndex request, current-term commit, or heartbeat acknowledgement',['S_proposal','S_ack','S_reads','S_read_release','S_read_queue','S_roles'],implementation_guards=['Non-singleton leaders postpone reads before a current-term commit.','Safe mode counts unique voter acknowledgements under current voter sets; caller differentiates requests by RequestCtx.'],writes=['Records committed read index and request context; acknowledged queued requests produce ReadStates or ReadIndexResp.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_authority','F_committed','F_config'],important_branches=['Singleton returns committed index directly; lease-based mode bypasses safe-mode heartbeat quorum.','Reset clears readOnly pending ack queue but not the separate pre-first-commit request list.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Consumes established commitment and quorum contact for safe read authority; caller still waits for state-machine application.'})\nF=[dict(id='F_authority',meaning='The node records a local term and role; becoming leader results from winning the configured vote quorum, while follower/pre-candidate states do not assert leader authority.',identity={'node':'raft.id','term':'raft.Term'},validity_context='Local role/term and current applied configuration; role can change without term change.',representation=['raft.Term','raft.Vote','raft.state','raft.lead','tracker.Votes'],invalidators=['B_context_reset'],reinterpreters=['B_configuration'],durability='Term and vote enter HardState and must be persisted; role, leader and tally are volatile.',recovery='newRaft reloads HardState/configuration and becomes follower.',source_ids=['S_campaign','S_dispatch','S_restore_init']),dict(id='F_committed',meaning='This local log records a committed prefix ending at committed. It does not assert completion of state-machine application or local persistence of every exposed entry.',identity={'node':'raft.id','prefix_end':'raftLog.committed'},validity_context='Log identity is index/term; commitment survives later terms. Leader advancement qualifies current-term quorum support; follower advancement uses leader matching-prefix evidence; recovery uses supplied persisted state.',representation=['raftLog.committed','HardState.Commit'],invalidators=[],reinterpreters=[],durability='HardState commit and log/snapshot persistence are caller duties; committed is an in-memory observation until processed.',recovery='Loaded HardState and snapshot reconstruct the prefix.',source_ids=['S_log_append','S_log_commit','S_log_context','S_config','S_restore_init','S_restore']),dict(id='F_config',meaning='The node currently uses the installed incoming/outgoing voter sets and learner roles; AutoLeave marks that Raft owns initiation of leaving this joint configuration. This fact does not assert that an exit proposal has been admitted.',identity={'node':'raft.id','configuration':'applied incoming/outgoing voters and learners'},validity_context='Until another applied configuration or restored snapshot replaces it; joint voters remain authoritative during any pending automatic exit.',representation=['tracker.Config.Voters','tracker.Config.Learners','tracker.Config.LearnersNext','tracker.Config.AutoLeave'],invalidators=['B_configuration','B_recovery'],reinterpreters=[],durability='Configuration is reflected in applied ConfState and snapshots, with committed entries for replay; volatile tracker state is not itself persistence.',recovery='confchange.Restore reconstructs voters and passes snapshot AutoLeave to EnterJoint.',source_ids=['S_conf_contract','S_confchange','S_tracker','S_restore_config'],unknowns=['Configuration export via Clone may omit AutoLeave without changing the active tracker.'])]\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nsummaries={'A1':'Leader proposals are replicated and durable support is aggregated using configured voters; current-term qualification controls commitment, which followers learn through matched append or bounded heartbeat commit.','A2':'Term/role changes, quorum elections and transfers acquire or revoke authority; reset discards volatile support but retains established log decisions.','A3':'In-repository restart and snapshot mechanisms reconstruct eligible history and configuration; persistence is caller-provided.','A4':'In-repository Changer validates simple/joint transitions; application determines activation and automatic exit ownership.','A5':'Committed Ready entries are consumed by the caller; in-repository accounting and completion responses determine subsequent application availability and joint-exit attempts.','A6':'In-repository Ready/worker-message scheduling enforces persistence dependencies, with caller-provided storage and recovery input.','A7':'Proposal admission does not guarantee commitment; read-index correlation and application waits are caller responsibilities, supported by library quorum-read processing.'}\naudit=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured go.etcd.io/raft/v3 library: raft state machine, Node/RawNode APIs, tracker/quorum, configuration changes, Ready and Storage interfaces. Network, durable storage implementation and user state machine are caller-owned; their library-facing duties remain applicable.',protocol_contexts=['One raft group with nonzero unique node IDs','Terms, log index/term identity, applied simple or joint voter configuration'],external_interfaces=['Node/RawNode Step, Tick, Ready, Advance, Propose, ApplyConfChange, TransferLeadership','Storage, HardState, snapshots and asynchronous local append/apply messages'],ownership=['Node serializes requests in its run loop; RawNode callers serialize access.','Caller supplies transport, persistence and ordered application.'],variants=['Conventional and asynchronous storage writes','PreVote, CheckQuorum, safe versus lease reads','Simple and joint configuration transitions'],source_ids=['S_usage','S_async_contract','S_node_contract','S_node_loop','S_raw_ready']),activities=[dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=roles[a]['relation'],realization_summary=summaries[a],source_ids=sorted(set(s for b in B if b['primary_activity']==a for s in b['source_ids']))) for a in roles],behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='tracker.Config.Clone -> getStatus',disposition='deferred',reason='Clone copies voter/learner maps but omits AutoLeave; getStatus uses the clone. Active Changer EnterJoint explicitly sets AutoLeave and LeaveJoint clears it, so export loss must not be conflated with active transition loss.',source_ids=['S_tracker','S_status','S_confchange']),dict(entry_point='raft.switchToConfig -> maybeCommit',disposition='deferred',reason='Configuration-driven commit does not release pending pre-first-commit reads; legal reachability must account for the campaign guard against unapplied committed configuration entries.',source_ids=['S_config','S_campaign','S_ack']),dict(entry_point='raft.appliedTo -> automatic joint exit',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_application','B_transfer','B_configuration'],reason='Specific continuation question selected; map association is not resolution.',source_ids=['S_auto_leave','S_timers','S_transfer'],high_consequence=True)],core_overview=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation and authority paths plus their supporting history, membership, recovery and completion boundaries have been traced. Local continuation and export anomalies remain open, not global readiness gaps.',formation=dict(explanation='A leader assigns index and term to accepted proposals and queues a self acknowledgement behind persistence. Followers verify the predecessor term, replace only an uncommitted conflicting suffix, and return append responses after storage processing. Leader Match values are aggregated over the applied configuration: joint configurations require both majorities, and maybeCommit additionally requires current-term log identity. Changed commitment is broadcast; follower heartbeats are capped at known Match. Ready exposes committed entries for ordered caller application, and completion advances applied separately from committed.',behavior_ids=['B_replication','B_storage_ready','B_application'],fact_ids=['F_committed','F_config','F_authority'],source_ids=['S_commit_reset','S_ack','S_receive','S_log_append','S_joint','S_raw_ready','S_raw_completion']),context=dict(explanation='Tick or explicit campaign begins an election only for an eligible voter without pending snapshots or committed unapplied configuration changes. Vote choice is conditioned on local vote/leader state and candidate log freshness, with persistence-dependent replies and joint quorum counting. Higher terms normally install follower state; pre-vote and lease checks qualify this rule. Reset clears volatile aggregation and read-ack context, transfer target and pending configuration index, while committed history remains. Leader transfer pauses proposals, catches up a voter and sends TimeoutNow; it aborts on timeout or membership removal. Configuration changes activate on application, and snapshots/restart reconstruct configuration and history.',behavior_ids=['B_election','B_context_reset','B_transfer','B_configuration','B_recovery'],fact_ids=['F_authority','F_config','F_committed'],source_ids=['S_campaign','S_dispatch','S_timers','S_roles','S_config','S_restore']),connection=dict(explanation='Applied voter membership supplies both election and replication quorum meaning. A new leader resets peer Match and conservatively postpones new configuration changes until its inherited log tail is applied; its empty current-term entry enables safe commitment of older history. Old network replies are filtered by term and role, while old storage append completion cannot stabilize overwritten entries. Committed application and snapshot completion remain term-independent. Pending reads waiting for a first current-term commit are distinct from the reset read-ack queue. Applied joint configurations continue to require outgoing and incoming quorums until a leave entry is committed and applied; application completion attempts automatic exit but transfer admission can reject that proposal.',behavior_ids=['B_election','B_context_reset','B_replication','B_configuration','B_application','B_storage_ready','B_reads'],fact_ids=['F_config','F_authority','F_committed'],source_ids=['S_campaign','S_dispatch','S_config','S_auto_leave','S_proposal','S_read_release']),open_details=['Automatic exit continuation after a failed leadership transfer with no new client proposals.','AutoLeave representation in status copies.','Legal reachability of pending-read release differences at configuration-driven commitment.','Deeper snapshot, flow-control and client cancellation variants are not fully mapped.'],core_gaps=[]))\njson.dump(audit,open('initial-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='When application completion attempts to leave an implicit joint configuration during a leadership transfer, does the same leader retain an implementation-owned continuation after the transfer times out, or can the active AutoLeave configuration remain without an exit proposal unless unrelated client work arrives?',importance='A stranded joint configuration can retain outgoing quorum requirements and prevent later membership changes; this is a potential configuration-progress consequence, not a measured safety violation.',source_ids=['S_auto_leave','S_timers','S_transfer','S_conf_contract','S_node_contract'],participants=['Current leader','Transfer target','Incoming and outgoing voters','Application/Ready owner'],objects=['Active joint configuration','Empty leave-joint proposal','leadTransferee','Applied/pendingConfIndex'],contexts=['Implicit joint transition already committed and applied','Transfer overlaps the completion callback that attempts automatic exit','Transfer times out while leader remains active and voter quorums communicate'],event_paths=['ApplyConfChange -> Advance/MsgStorageApplyResp -> appliedTo -> MsgProp rejected due to leadTransferee','Tick -> tickHeartbeat -> abortLeaderTransfer; future heartbeat/Ready processing'],activity_classes=['A4','A2'],behavior_ids=['B_configuration','B_application','B_transfer'],fact_ids=['F_config'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_storage_ready':'Determines which caller completion events invoke appliedTo and whether another such event is guaranteed.','B_replication':'Establishes committed configuration entry and can create later application callbacks.','B_election':'A successful transfer/new leader creates a new entry, an alternative continuation outside the failed-transfer case.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['appliedTo retries on later applied entries.','Successful transfer gives a new leader an empty entry and a later completion opportunity.','Client proposals may be retried by callers, but ownership of the internal implicit-exit retry must be distinguished.'],unknowns=['Does ordinary heartbeat-only Ready/Advance processing after timeout invoke appliedTo when it has no committed entries?','Construct one legal prefix with the joint entry fully committed and applied, transfer still active at its completion callback, and no guaranteed later application work.','Determine the precise automatic-exit duty and scheduling assumptions without inventing a numeric deadline.'],trigger_rationale='The source explicitly allows transfer to reject the internal exit attempt, while its timeout only clears leadTransferee. A small deterministic RawNode schedule can distinguish ordinary completion retry from dependence on a new application entry. This progress premise is more consequential than the separate status-copy omission and more directly sourced than the uncertain config-commit read-release history.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\njson.dump(dict(action='continue',rationale='Record the initial two-core-line map and select a sourced continuation question. No execution or defect attribution is claimed.',sources=sources,map_path='initial-map.json',question=q),open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_initial.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
